Subject: Add dispatch mode to `why3find prove`

Purpose: `why3find prove --dispatch` keeps goal generation, the proof
  strategy, tactics and the proof files in why3find, and sends every prover
  call and every access to the prover cache to the parent process over stdin
  and stdout. It also answers the parent's requests to print a goal with a
  prover's driver after a list of transformations (with the number of tasks),
  to print a goal's task, to list the provers with their commands and input
  file extensions, to read a prover's answer from a recorded output with the
  prover's driver, and to report a prover's calibration. Without the option, behaviour is unchanged.
  The message grammar is documented in src/dispatch.mli.
Requirements: R1.2, R1.3, R2.3, R7.2, R7.5, R7.9, R7.12
Upstream: not yet submitted
Base: https://github.com/creusot-rs/why3find commit 89dd8721fb9de7fea5d00e58ebdabdc75a8235b8
